{"id":"sign-of-a-huge-product","lc":"sign-of-the-product-of-an-array","title":"Sign of a Huge Product","diff":"easy","pattern":"math-geometry","tags":["math","counting"],"statement":"<p>You get an integer array <code>nums</code>. Imagine multiplying all of its values together. Return the <b>sign</b> of that product: <code>1</code> if it is positive, <code>-1</code> if it is negative, and <code>0</code> if it is zero.</p>\n<p>The product itself can be far too large for a normal number, so work out the sign without computing it.</p>","examples":[{"in":"nums = [-3, 5, -2, 7]","out":"1","why":"Two negative factors cancel out: the product is 210."},{"in":"nums = [4, -1, 0, -6]","out":"0","why":"One zero makes the whole product zero, whatever else is in the array."},{"in":"nums = [-2, -2, -2]","out":"-1","why":"Three negative factors: an odd count, so the product (−8) is negative."}],"constraints":["1 ≤ nums.length ≤ 100 000","−100 ≤ nums[i] ≤ 100"],"fn":{"name":"productSign","params":[["nums","int[]"]],"returns":"int"},"tests":[{"args":[[-3,5,-2,7]],"expected":1},{"args":[[4,-1,0,-6]],"expected":0},{"args":[[-2,-2,-2]],"expected":-1},{"args":[[5]],"expected":1},{"args":[[-5]],"expected":-1},{"args":[[0]],"expected":0},{"args":[[1,1,1,1]],"expected":1},{"args":[[-1,-1,-1,-1]],"expected":1},{"args":[[0,-1]],"expected":0},{"args":[[-1,0]],"expected":0},{"args":[[-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-100,-10